# Build output.
/forge
/bin/

# Coverage and profiling artefacts. Anchored to a module root so that test
# fixtures keep their extensions — which is why the nested module needs its own
# line rather than being covered by the one above.
/cover.out
/coverage.out
/x/csv/cover.out
/*.prof
*.test

# A workspace applies to everybody who clones, which would put every build on
# this tree rather than on what the nested modules' go.mod files actually
# require — so a requirement nobody outside can resolve would keep working here
# and fail for them. It is the local tool that replaces those replace
# directives once there is a version to require; see docs/releasing.md.
/go.work
/go.work.sum

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# A bare "tags" is the usual global ignore for ctags output, and it also matches
# this module's internal/tags package directory. Re-include it here.
/tags
!internal/tags/

# Claude Code keeps its worktrees here. A worktree is a checkout, and a
# `git add .` in the main checkout picks one up as a gitlink.
/.claude/worktrees/

# The design document and the work breakdown are kept beside this checkout
# rather than in it, and a `git add .` has already committed them once.
/prd.md
/tasks.md
